        "original_id": "e438716d-d015-5622-ac70-c0cadef5af17",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph A. Loftus; George P. Shultz\n- Organizations: The New York Times; International Brotherhood of Teamsters; U.S. Department of Labor; U.S. Department of the Treasury\n- Roles: reporter; communications assistant\n- Topics: unions\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph A. Loftus was born in 1907 and died in 1990.\n- George P. Shultz was born on December 13, 1920.\n- Joseph A. Loftus was a 20th-century American reporter for The New York Times.\n- Joseph A. Loftus covered unions extensively, including the International Brotherhood of Teamsters.\n- Joseph A. Loftus later worked as a communications assistant to George P. Shultz at the U.S. Department of Labor and the U.S. Department of the Treasury.\n- George P. Shultz is an American economist, statesman, and businessman.",
